 26. Additional issues (16 to 24)

16. Accessibility Issue:** Missing page title or page language
- Who May Be Affected:** Screen reader users, people using translation tools
- Explanation of the Barrier:** Without a title, users cannot tell tabs apart. Without a language tag, screen readers may pronounce words wrongly.
- Practical Improvement:** Give every page a unique `<title>` and add `<html lang="en">`.

17. Accessibility Issue:** PDFs and documents that are scanned images
- Who May Be Affected:** Blind and low-vision users, people on low-end phones
- Explanation of the Barrier:** Screen readers cannot read a scanned page, and the text cannot be resized or searched.
- Practical Improvement:** Publish text-based, tagged PDFs, or provide an HTML version.

18. Accessibility Issue:** Text embedded in images
- Who May Be Affected:** Low-vision users, screen reader users
- Explanation of the Barrier:** Text in a banner or poster cannot be resized, recoloured or read aloud.
- Practical Improvement:** Use real HTML text. If an image of text is unavoidable, repeat the text in the alt text.

19. Accessibility Issue:** Data tables without headers
- Who May Be Affected:** Screen reader users
- Explanation of the Barrier:** Without header cells, users hear numbers with no idea which row or column they belong to.
- Practical Improvement:** Use `<th scope="col">` and `<th scope="row">`, and add a `<caption>`.

20. Accessibility Issue:** CAPTCHA with no alternative
- Who May Be Affected:** Blind, low-vision and cognitive-disability users
- Explanation of the Barrier:** Distorted-text or image puzzles cannot be solved by many users.
- Practical Improvement:** Offer an audio or logic-based alternative, or use invisible bot checks.

**21. Accessibility Issue:** Inconsistent navigation
- **Who May Be Affected:** Cognitive-disability users, screen reader users, first-time visitors
- **Explanation of the Barrier:** Menus that change position or order between pages make the site hard to learn.
- **Practical Improvement:** Keep menus, labels and layout the same on every page.

22. Accessibility Issue:** No "Skip to main content" link
- **Who May Be Affected:** Keyboard and screen reader users
- **Explanation of the Barrier:** They must Tab through the whole menu on every page.
- **Practical Improvement:** Add a skip link as the first focusable element.

23. Accessibility Issue:** Pop-ups and modals that trap keyboard focus
- **Who May Be Affected:** Keyboard and screen reader users
- **Explanation of the Barrier:** Focus enters the pop-up and cannot leave, or the pop-up cannot be closed with Esc.
- **Practical Improvement:** Move focus into the modal, allow Esc to close it, and return focus to the trigger button.

24. Accessibility Issue:** Drag-only actions and tiny tap targets
- **Who May Be Affected:** People with tremors or motor disabilities, mobile users
- **Explanation of the Barrier:** Sliders and drag-and-drop need precise movement, and small buttons are easy to miss.
- **Practical Improvement:** Provide a click or button alternative to dragging, and make targets at least 24×24 px (44×44 px is better).

